.Dd June 10, 2026
.Dt ZDOTS-SERVER-KEYS 1
.Os zdots
.Sh NAME
.Nm zdots-server-keys
.Nd environment-scoped SSH key management for server access
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar environment
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
generates and manages
.Xr ssh-keygen 1
ed25519 key pairs scoped to deployment environments
.Pq staging, production ,
installs them on remote hosts via
.Xr ssh-copy-id 1 ,
and maintains the corresponding
.Xr ssh_config 5
stanzas in
.Pa ~/.ssh/config .
.Pp
It is the server-access counterpart to
.Xr zdots-github-keys 1 ,
which manages GitHub identity keys.
Both tools share the same command vocabulary
.Pq plan / apply / status / rotate-stage / rotate-promote / public-key
and the same
.Pa id_{slug}@{org}
key-naming convention, so key families behave consistently across GitHub
and server contexts.
.Pp
.Nm
is a
.Em zdots
tool, not an adots tool.
adots is a configuration-facilitating layer; it may export the
.Ev ZDOTS_SERVER_ORG
and
.Ev ZDOTS_SERVER_USER
environment variables to customise defaults, but no key logic lives
inside adots itself.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width rotate-promote
.It Ic plan
Display key paths, public-key comments, and SSH config stanzas for all
environments without writing anything.
Pass
.Fl -host
to preview stanzas with specific hostnames.
.It Ic apply Fl -yes
Generate ed25519 key pairs for both environments and append their Host blocks
to
.Pa ~/.ssh/config .
Idempotent: a stanza is never written twice.
Requires
.Fl -yes
because it mutates
.Pa ~/.ssh/config .
.It Ic status
Report the on-disk presence of every active and staged key file and the
SSH config file.
Read-only.
.It Ic copy-id Ar env
Run
.Xr ssh-copy-id 1
to install the public key for
.Ar env
on each host named with
.Fl -host .
The host must already be reachable (password or existing key).
.It Ic rotate-stage Ar env
Generate a staged candidate key at
.Pa ~/.ssh/id_{slug}@{org}.next
without touching the active key or the SSH config stanza.
Install the staged public key on target hosts before promoting.
.It Ic rotate-promote Ar env Fl -yes
Replace the active key with the staged
.Pa .next
key by renaming both the private and public key files.
The SSH config stanza is unchanged; it already references the stable
.Pa id_{slug}@{org}
path.
Requires
.Fl -yes .
Test connectivity before revoking the old key on each host.
.It Ic public-key Ar selector
Print the public key for
.Ar selector
to stdout.
.Ar selector
is an environment name
.Pq Ic staging , Ic production
or a staged variant
.Pq Ic staging_next , Ic production_next .
Useful for piping to
.Xr pbcopy 1
or pasting into
.Pa authorized_keys .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl -org Ar org
Organisation slug embedded in key names
.Pq default: Li work No or Ev ZDOTS_SERVER_ORG .
.It Fl -user Ar user
Remote username written into the SSH config stanza and passed to
.Xr ssh-copy-id 1
.Pq default: current OS user or Ev ZDOTS_SERVER_USER .
.It Fl -host Ar host
Hostname to include in the SSH config
.Ic Host
line and to target with
.Ic copy-id .
Repeatable.
.It Fl -key-type Ar type
Key algorithm passed to
.Xr ssh-keygen 1
.Pq default: Li ed25519 No or Ev ZDOTS_SERVER_KEY_TYPE .
.It Fl -yes
Required guard for commands that write to
.Pa ~/.ssh/config
or rename key files
.Pq Ic apply , Ic rotate-promote .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show usage.
.El
.Sh KEY NAMING CONVENTION
Keys follow the pattern
.Pa id_{slug}@{org}
stored in
.Pa ~/.ssh :
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width production -compact
.It staging
.Pa ~/.ssh/id_staging@work
.It production
.Pa ~/.ssh/id_prod@work
.It staged
.Pa ~/.ssh/id_{slug}@work.next
.El
.Pp
The
.Pa .next
suffix keeps staged keys adjacent to their active counterparts and mirrors
the
.Xr github-keygen 1
rotation convention.
.Sh ROTATION WORKFLOW
Key rotation replaces the active key without a window of lost access:
.Bl -enum
.It
.Dl zdots-server-keys rotate-stage staging
Generate
.Pa ~/.ssh/id_staging@work.next .
.It
.Dl zdots-server-keys copy-id staging --host staging
Install the staged public key on each host alongside the existing key.
.It
Verify the staged key works:
.Dl ssh -i ~/.ssh/id_staging@work.next user@staging
.It
.Dl zdots-server-keys rotate-promote staging --yes
Rename
.Pa .next
to the active path.
.It
Revoke the old public key from
.Pa authorized_keys
on each host.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ZDOTS_SERVER_KEY_TYPE
.It Ev ZDOTS_SERVER_ORG
Organisation slug used in key names
.Pq default: Li work .
.It Ev ZDOTS_SERVER_USER
Remote username for SSH config and
.Xr ssh-copy-id 1
.Pq default: current OS user .
.It Ev ZDOTS_SERVER_KEY_TYPE
Key algorithm for
.Xr ssh-keygen 1
.Pq default: Li ed25519 .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa ~/.ssh/id_staging@work
Active private key for staging hosts.
.It Pa ~/.ssh/id_staging@work.pub
Active public key for staging hosts.
.It Pa ~/.ssh/id_prod@work
Active private key for production hosts.
.It Pa ~/.ssh/id_prod@work.pub
Active public key for production hosts.
.It Pa ~/.ssh/id_{slug}@work.next
Staged rotation candidate
.Pq present only during an in-progress rotation .
.It Pa ~/.ssh/config
Receives
.Ic Host
blocks appended by
.Ic apply .
Each block is guarded by a comment marker for idempotency.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Preview what
.Ic apply
would create, including the SSH config stanzas for staging:
.Pp
.Dl zdots-server-keys plan --host staging
.Pp
Generate both environment keys and wire up
.Pa ~/.ssh/config
with staging as the staging host:
.Pp
.Dl zdots-server-keys apply --yes --host staging
.Pp
Push the staging key to staging:
.Pp
.Dl zdots-server-keys copy-id staging --host staging
.Pp
Push the production key to two hosts under a different login:
.Pp
.Dl zdots-server-keys copy-id production --host web1 --host web2 --user deploy
.Pp
Print the staging public key to the clipboard:
.Pp
.Dl zdots-server-keys public-key staging | pbcopy
.Pp
Stage a new staging key for rotation, install it, then promote:
.Pp
.Dl zdots-server-keys rotate-stage staging
.Dl ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/id_staging@work.next user@staging
.Dl zdots-server-keys rotate-promote staging --yes
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zdots-github-keys 1 ,
.Xr ssh-keygen 1 ,
.Xr ssh-copy-id 1 ,
.Xr ssh_config 5 ,
.Xr zdots 7
